==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈr̥iɲca/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iɲca|lang=is}}

===Verb===
'''hringja''' (+ {{dative}}; ''weak conjugation:'' [[hringdi]] – [[hringt]])

# to [[phone]], to [[call]] almost always used with ''[[í#Icelandic|í]]'' (then followed by + {{accusative}})
#* ''[[ég#Icelandic|Ég]] '''hringi''' [[í#Icelandic|í]] [[þig#Icelandic|þig]] ({{accusative}}) [[þegar]] [[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[vera#Icelandic|er]] [[búinn]] [[með#Icelandic|með]] [[matur|matinn]].''
#*: (lit. I'll '''call''' you when I am done with the food.)
#*:: [[I'll]] '''call''' [[you]] [[when]] [[I've]] [[finished]] [[eating]].
# to [[ring]] (a doorbell)
#* ''[[ætla|Ætlar]] [[þú#Icelandic|þú]] að '''hringja''' ([[dyr]]a)[[bjalla#Icelandic|bjöllunni]] ({{dative}}).''
#*: [[shall|Shall]] [[you]] '''ring''' the ([[door]])[[bell]]?

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to phone}} [[hringja í]]
* {{sense|ring}} [[dingla]]

